<title>FRANCE: Renault sees French 97 vehicle regs at 1.9-2.0 mln.</title>
<headline>Renault sees French 97 vehicle regs at 1.9-2.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chairman of French carmaker Renault said in a newspaper interview that after &quot;difficult months&quot; linked to the end of a government car buying incentive scheme, French car registrations may reach 1.9 to 2.0 million vehicles units in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We are bound to have some difficult months; many customers have advanced by a few weeks or a few months their purchases. We think that the French (car) market in 1997 will be between 1.9 and 2.0 million vehicles,&quot; Louis Schweitzer told Le Figaro.</p>
</text>
